<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippine Jan trade deficit rises to $1.145 bln.</title>
<headline>Philippine Jan trade deficit rises to $1.145 bln.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine merchandise trade deficit rose to $1.145 billion in January compared with $816 million a year ago, the National Statistics Office said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>In December 1996, the country posted a trade deficit of $835 million.  </p>
<p>    MERCHANDISE TRADE    Jan 97  Dec 96  Jan 96</p>
<p>    Exports		   1.692   1.883   1.420</p>
<p>    Imports		   2.837   2.718   2.236</p>
<p>    Trade balance	  -1.145  -0.835  -0.816</p>
<p>Note - Figures are in U.S. dollar billion.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom +63 2 8109636 Fax 8176267</p>
</text>
